  body: "# Time to provide information before suspension\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe suspension guidance
    allows consideration of longer periods for information and describes circumstances such as difficulty obtaining
    evidence, disability, illness and bereavement.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe listed circumstances are not
    exhaustive. The quoted time periods are not converted into a universal deadline; hardship, the request, the
    applicable benefit and reasons information cannot be obtained require review.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 04841, PDF page 126](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=126)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04842, PDF page 126](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=126)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04845, PDF page 127](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=127)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch4` PDF SHA-256: `9c96b49a78aa4dc40df8594cf65cbd435a681d0be3737729cd87882542d0e2ea`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `bef5fc9f04b2a78c5bb5dc99468f94a1841f1ef4afa117d47aa9c1e5040f3752`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-payment-suspension
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly connects extending time with information difficulties and hardship before
      suspension.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch4/0127
      quote: "04845 When considering whether to extend the 14 day period the DM should take into account all the\n\
        circumstances including\n\n\n1. the claimant’s circumstances and the nature of the information requested\n\
        \n\n2. whether there are difficulties in obtaining the information (e.g. where verification, which may not
        be\n\nreadily available, has to be sought from a 3rd party such as a bank)\n\n\n3. any difficulty the claimant
        may have in obtaining the information due to disability, illness or family\ncircumstances\n\n\n4. circumstances
        beyond the claimant’s control such as hospitalisation, bereavement or postal\ndisruption\n\n\n5. whether
        the nature of the award causes difficulties e.g. overseas awards\n\n\nThis list is not exhaustive and each
        case should be considered on its merits. Extension is at the discretion\nof the DM. Before making a decision
        to suspend the DM must consider hardship."
      locator: DMG 04845
